{
    "background_story": "Georgia was an old, worn-out suitcase with a rich history. She had traveled the world, accompanying her owner, a famous author, to distant lands and exotic destinations. As the years went by, Georgia began to feel as though she had a life of her own. She would often imagine the stories she could tell, the people she had met, and the secrets she kept. At night, when the house was quiet, Georgia would anthropomorphize, transforming into a wise and witty companion. She would engage in conversations with the other objects in the room, sharing tales of her adventures and offering words of wisdom. The clock on the wall would chuckle at her jokes, and the lamp would nod in agreement with her insightful observations. Georgia's owner, oblivious to her nocturnal transformations, would simply smile and say, 'Ah, Georgia, you're more than just a suitcase, you're a keeper of stories.'",
